  "padua-far": {
   "name": "Padua",
   "wikidata": "Q617",
   "editions": 135,
   "unesco": true,
   "dayTripListed": true,
   "sights": [
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Saint Anthony's cathedral",
     "lat": 45.401364,
     "lng": 11.880069,
     "hours": "Every day, 6.20 - 19.00 (DST 19.45)",
     "price": "Free entrance",
     "wikidata": "Q810139",
     "content": "Saint Anthony's Basilica is the best-known tourist site in Padova - millions of pilgrims visit every year. Built immediately after \"The Saint's\" death in the 1200s, it houses his tomb and notable relics. The statues and crucifix on the main",
     "editions": 38
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Scrovegni Chapel",
     "lat": 45.411667,
     "lng": 11.879444,
     "hours": "Every day, 9.00-19.00",
     "price": "€14 full price, €5 student price (''including Eremitani Civic Museum and Contemporary Art Museum'')",
     "wikidata": "Q963954",
     "content": "The Chapel is in the north of the city center, not far from the bus and train stations. The walls and ceilings are covered in frescos by Giotto, completed in 1303-1305. The chapel has been well preserved and the art is very impressive. Some",
     "editions": 38
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Astronomic Observatory",
     "lat": 45.401972,
     "lng": 11.868415,
     "hours": "Sat-Sun 11.00-16.00 (18.00 May-Oct)",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q3966414",
     "content": "Although the observatory was built after Galileo's time in Padua, you'll learn a lot about his significance for the research in Padua. You reach the top of the tower after a lecture of about one hour and can enjoy the view. ''Tickets at the",
     "editions": 9
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Palazzo della Ragione",
     "lat": 45.407222,
     "lng": 11.875278,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q2517428",
     "content": "The large building located between Piazza della Frutta and Piazza delle Erbe. Its ground floor hosts small market shops. The upper floor is a single large hall housing artwork and occasional exhibitions.",
     "editions": 17
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Palazzo del Bo'",
     "lat": 45.40684,
     "lng": 11.87754,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q3360829",
     "content": "",
     "editions": 11
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Botanic Garden",
     "lat": 45.398889,
     "lng": 11.880556,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q598892",
     "content": "The world's oldest still operating botanic garden, operated by the University of Padua, and on the UNESCO World Heritage list since 1997. It is not large, but is subtly laid out to swallow groups of people and give the impression of solitud",
     "editions": 40,
     "unesco": true
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Eremitani Civic Museum",
     "lat": 45.41096,
     "lng": 11.88001,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q3867519",
     "content": "The museum is divided into an archeological section and a picture gallery, which has a very important collection with Tizian, Tintoretto, Giotto and Bellini among other important painters.",
     "editions": 5
    }
   ],
